35,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"My observations confirm a problem. The morning rush is a shoving match, and some spots are exposed to rain, making them less desirable.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The financial reality is that we have no dedicated budget for this. Any new system requiring maintenance will need a new levy.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,My findings are troubling. The same flats have held the best spots for five years without any formal review or vote. It's no wonder people are grumbling.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It seems we have a mix of stagnant privilege and passive-aggressive complaints. If we just shuffle spots randomly, we might ignite a war.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"I found out that the current cash collection already takes three hours a month! If we make the system more complex, someone will just quit!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@George, that explains the tension. But we must prioritize the physical flow. If we don't fix the congestion, the ""best"" spots will still be a mess.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Mio, three hours a month is already inefficient. If we introduce a complex billing system to cover costs, the administrative burden will become unsustainable.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"I agree with @Asuka that flow matters, but we cannot ignore the lack of transparency. A fair system must start with a clean slate.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"A clean slate sounds noble, but it's often a recipe for resentment. We need a solution that doesn't turn the lobby into a cold zone.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"I'm worried! If we add more paperwork to those three hours, the next person in charge will just give up like the last two did!","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"We need a system that minimizes the need for constant management while solving the physical bottleneck. A fixed, logical rotation could work.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A rotation is simple, but it doesn't address the cost of maintenance. If we don't charge for the spaces, the building account remains stagnant.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"A rotation would certainly remove the perception of favoritism. It treats every resident as an equal, regardless of how long they've lived here.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Rotation is rational, provided it's not so frequent that it becomes a chore. We don't want people fighting over the ""best"" month.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"As long as the rotation doesn't require a mountain of paperwork every month, I'm for it! Let's keep it super simple!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
